// ============================================================
// Canonical Domain (L5) — a target model fed by M2M, not by a store
// ============================================================
// The chain is relational -> source model -> M2M -> canonical model. A firm's canonical
// model is rarely mapped straight onto tables; it is derived from whatever the source
// systems produce, and the derivation is where the interesting mistakes live.
//
// This is the fourth invariance: the canonical class carries the SAME facts as
// trading::Trade, reached through an entirely different execution path -- the M2M engine
// rather than SQL. It must agree.
###Pure
Class canonical::CanonicalTrade
{
    // Renamed on the way through, so a mapping that silently passed the source object
    // along unchanged would not satisfy the projection.
    identifier: String[1];
    executedOn: StrictDate[1];
    grossValue: Float[1];
    // Computed in the M2M layer, not read from a column: the source has quantity and
    // price, the canonical model has their product and nothing else.
    unitPrice: Float[1];
    units: Float[1];
    side: trading::Side[1];
    state: String[1];
}
